\h 2 THESSALONIANS
\toc1 2 Thessalonians
\toc2 2 Thessalonians
\toc3 2Th
\mt2 This book is one of the letters that the Apostle Paul wrote to the Christians at Thessalonica. We call this book
\mt1 2 Thessalonians
\c 1
\s1 2 Thessalonians 1:1-2
\s1 We, Paul, Silas, and Timothy, are sending this letter to the congregation of God’s people in Thessalonica. We pray that God will continue to bless you with his kindness and inner peace.
\p
\v 1  \add I\add*, Paul, \add am writing this letter\add*. Silas and Timothy \add are with me. We are sending this letter\add* to \add you\add*. You are the congregation \add of God’s people\add* in Thessalonica \add city\add*. You belong to God our Father, and you belong to Jesus Christ our Lord.
\v 2  \add We pray that\add* God our Father, and Jesus Christ our Lord, \add will continue to\add* act kindly toward you and \add will continue to cause you to have inner\add* peace.
\s1 We thank God very frequently that you are trusting in the Lord Jesus more and more.
\sr 2 Thessalonians 1:3-4
\p
\v 3  \add Our\add* fellow believers, we thank God very frequently [HYP] for you because we believers ought \add to thank God for each other, and\add* specifically it is appropriate/right \add that we should thank God for you. We thank him\add* that you are trusting in \add the Lord Jesus\add* more and more, and that each one of you is loving \add each of\add* the others more and more.
\v 4 As a result, we keep proudly telling about you to \add other\add* congregations who \add worship\add* God. \add Specifically, we tell them\add* that you are being steadfast and that you \add continue\add* believing \add in the Lord Jesus\add*, even though you are frequently suffering [DOU] as a result of people causing you trouble.
\s1 God will judge all people justly. Specifically, he will publicly declare that you are worthy to enter that place where he will rule his people forever.
\sr 2 Thessalonians 1:5-10
\p
\v 5  \add Your being steadfast\add* ◄shows/indicates to► \add us\add* clearly that God will judge \add all people\add* justly. \add Specifically, he\add* will publicly declare that you are worthy \add as his people to be in\add* that place where he will rule \add forever, because\add* you also are suffering as a result of \add telling others about letting\add* God rule your lives.
\v 6  \add God will certainly cause trouble for\add* those people who are troubling you, because he \add considers\add* that it is just that he should punish such people for doing that to you.
\v 7 He also \add considers\add* that it is the right thing to do to reward you who are being troubled, by ◄giving you relief/causing your suffering to end►. He will do that for both you and us when our Lord Jesus will descend from heaven, together with his powerful angels and with blazing fire.
\v 8  \add Then he will\add* punish those people who do not \add want to\add* know him and \add those\add* who refuse to heed the message about our Lord Jesus.
\v 9  \add Our Lord Jesus\add* will forbid them from ever coming near to him and near to the glory which he has \add because he is so\add* powerful (OR, the glory that is manifested by his power). He will cause those people to suffer forever.
\v 10  \add The Lord Jesus\add* will do this when he comes \add back from heaven\add* at the time \add that God has decided\add*. As a result, all we who are his people will praise him because of \add what he has done for his own\add* people, and all we believers will marvel at our Lord because of \add what he has done. And you will be there, too\add*, because you believed what we testified to you.
\s1 We are praying very frequently for you that God will consider you worthy to receive that to which he summoned you.
\sr 2 Thessalonians 1:11-12
\p
\v 11 In order that you might \add praise Jesus like this\add*, we are also praying very frequently [HYP] for you. We pray that \add you will be able to show\add* our God that you are worthy \add to receive\add* that which he chose \add you to receive\add*. We pray also that he would powerfully enable you to do good in every way that you desire, and that he would also enable you to do powerfully every \add good\add* thing \add that you do because\add* you believe \add in Jesus Christ\add*.
\v 12  \add We pray this because we want\add* you to praise our Lord Jesus, and we want him to honor you. This will happen because God, whom we \add worship/serve\add*, and our Lord Jesus Christ will keep acting kindly \add toward you\add* in ways that you do not deserve.
\c 2
\s1 Do not quickly get worried and alarmed by any message that the Day of the Lord has already come.
\sr 2 Thessalonians 2:1-3a
\p
\v 1 Now \add I want to write to you\add* about the time when our Lord Jesus Christ will return and when \add God\add* will gather us together to \add where Jesus\add* is. My fellow believers, I urge you
\v 2 that you think calmly \add about any message\add* that \add claims/says\add* that the Lord has \add already\add* come again. Do not be shaken or alarmed/worried by any such message. \add It does not matter\add* if \add it is a message that someone claims God’s Spirit\add* revealed to him, or if \add it is some other message that someone\add* has spoken, or whether \add it is a message that someone claims\add* that I wrote in a letter.
\v 3 Do not allow anyone to deceive you in any way \add with the result that you believe any such message\add*.
\s1 The Lord will come only after that time when the man who will sin very greatly will appear.
\sr 2 Thessalonians 2:3b-5
\p \add The Lord\add* will not come [MTY] \add immediately\add*. First, \add many people\add* [PRS] will rebel \add against God\add*. The result of their rebelling will be that \add they will accept and obey\add* the man who will sin very greatly \add against God\add*.
\v 4 He will be the \add supreme\add* enemy \add of God\add*. He will \add proudly\add* exalt himself above everything that \add people\add* consider to be some god and above everything that people worship. \add As a result of wanting people to worship him\add*, he will \add even enter\add* God’s Temple and sit down \add there to rule\add*. He will publicly proclaim that he himself is God! But \add God\add* will \add certainly\add* punish that man forever!
\v 5 ◄I am sure that you remember that I kept telling you these things while I was still with you \add there in Thessalonica\add*./Do you not remember that I continued telling you these things while I was still with you \add there in Thessalonica\add*?► [RHQ]
\s1 This man will be revealed by God when he who is now preventing him from being revealed will have been removed by God.
\sr 2 Thessalonians 2:6-8
\p
\v 6 You also know that there is something (OR, someone) that is preventing this man \add from being revealed\add* {\add from revealing himself\add*}. This man is being ◄held back/restrained► \add now\add* for him to be revealed {that he reveal himself} at the time that \add God has planned\add* [MTY].
\v 7  \add Although Satan\add* is already secretly causing \add people\add* to reject \add God’s\add* laws, ◄the one/God► who is preventing \add this man from revealing himself\add* now \add will continue to prevent him from doing that\add* until he/\add God\add* removes him.
\v 8 It is then that \add God will allow\add* this man, who rejects \add God’s\add* laws \add completely\add*, to be revealed {to reveal himself}. Then the Lord Jesus will destroy him, by simply commanding it [MTY]. Jesus, by his own glorious arrival, will cause him to become \add completely\add* powerless.
\s1 When this man is present, he will completely deceive those who will perish.
\sr 2 Thessalonians 2:9-12
\p
\v 9 But \add before Jesus destroys him\add*, Satan will make him very powerful. As a result, he \add will do all kinds of supernatural\add* miracles and amazing things [DOU] that will seem as though \add God has enabled him to do them\add*.
\v 10 And by doing wicked \add things\add*, he will completely deceive those who will \add certainly\add* ◄perish/go to hell►. \add He will deceive them\add* because they will have refused to love the true \add message\add*. So they will not be saved {God will not save them}.
\v 11 So, God, by his power, will enable this man to easily deceive people, so that they will believe what \add this man\add* falsely \add claims/says that he is\add*.
\v 12 The result will be that everyone will be \add rightly\add* condemned {that \add God\add* will \add justly\add* condemn everyone} \add to be punished\add* who did not believe the true \add message\add*, but who instead gladly chose \add to be doing\add* what is wicked.
\s1 God chose you in order that you should be saved and share in Christ’s glory.
\sr 2 Thessalonians 2:13-14
\p
\v 13  \add Our\add* fellow believers, whom our Lord \add Jesus\add* loves, we thank God very frequently for you. It is appropriate/right for us to do that, because God chose you ◄from the beginning [MTY] \add of creation/before the world existed\add*► in order that he might save \add you\add* as a result of \add your\add* believing the true \add message\add* and as a result of \add God’s\add* Spirit setting you apart \add for God\add*.
\v 14  \add We thank God that\add* he chose you as a result of our \add proclaiming\add* the message about Christ \add to you\add*, in order that you might ◄share in/have► some of the glory that our Lord Jesus Christ has.
\s1 Continue believing the teaching that we gave to you.
\sr 2 Thessalonians 2:15
\p
\v 15 So, \add our fellow believers, continue to be firm concerning what you believe\add*; that is, continue believing the \add true\add* teaching that we gave to you by our speaking to you and by our \add writing\add* a letter \add to you\add*.
\s1 We pray that our Lord Jesus Christ himself will encourage you and cause you to continue doing and speaking what is good.
\sr 2 Thessalonians 2:16-17
\p
\v 16 Our Lord Jesus Christ himself and God, our Father, loves us and encourages us and causes us to confidently expect \add to receive\add* the eternal things that \add he has promised to give to us\add* as a result of \add Christ\add* acting kindly toward us in a way we did not deserve.
\v 17  \add We strongly pray that\add* God and Jesus together will encourage you! And we pray that they will cause you to continue doing and saying things that God considers to be good.
\c 3
\s1 Pray that more and more people will believe the message about our Lord Jesus.
\sr 2 Thessalonians 3:1-2
\p
\v 1 As for the other matters, \add our\add* fellow believers, pray for us that more and more \add people will\add* hear [PRS] our message \add about our\add* Lord \add Jesus\add*. Pray that they will believe this message, as you \add have done\add*.
\v 2 Pray also for us that we will be rescued {that God will rescue us} from those very perverse/evil people \add here\add* who \add cause us to suffer. Pray like that\add* because \add they and many others\add* refuse to believe [LIT] \add this message\add*.
\s1 Our Lord Jesus will cause you to continue to be steadfast and he will protect you from the evil one.
\sr 2 Thessalonians 3:3-5
\p
\v 3  \add Remember that our\add* Lord \add Jesus\add* is trustworthy! \add So we are sure that\add* he will cause you to continue to be steadfast. \add We are also sure that\add* he will protect you from \add Satan\add*, the evil one (OR, from evil).
\v 4  \add Because of your close relationship with our\add* Lord \add Jesus\add*, we are confident that you are obeying what we have commanded you, and we are confident that you will obey what we are commanding \add you in this letter\add*.
\v 5  \add We pray that our\add* Lord \add Jesus\add* would enable you to continue \add knowing\add* that God loves you. \add We pray\add* also that Christ will cause you to continue \add being\add* steadfast (OR, being steadfast as he \add was steadfast\add*).
\s1 We command you to disassociate yourselves from every fellow believer who refuses to work.
\sr 2 Thessalonians 3:6-11
\p
\v 6  \add Our\add* fellow believers, we command you, with the authority [MTY] that our Lord Jesus Christ \add has given to us\add*, that you stop associating with every fellow believer who is lazy and refuses to work. That is, you must stay away from those who are not \add conducting their lives\add* in the manner that we taught you.
\v 7  \add We tell you this\add* because you yourselves know that you should \add behave\add* like we \add behaved\add*. We ◄did not just sit \add around\add* without working/were never lazy► \add while we were living\add* among you.
\v 8 Specifically, we did not eat anyone’s food if we did not pay \add that person\add* for it. Instead, we worked very hard ◄\add to support ourselves/to earn the money to buy what we needed\add*►. We worked hard [DOU] during the day and during the night, in order that we would not have to depend on any of you \add to supply what we needed\add*.
\v 9 We have always had the right \add to depend on you for money, but instead we worked hard in order to make ourselves\add* examples for you, in order that you should behave like we behave.
\v 10 Remember that when we were \add there\add* with you, we kept commanding you that if any \add fellow believer\add* refuses to work, \add you should not give\add* him food to eat.
\v 11  \add We are commanding the same thing\add* again now, because someone has told us that some of you are lazy and not working at all, just interfering \add with what other people are doing\add*!
\s1 We command those fellow believers who are not working to support themselves by settling down and working.
\sr 2 Thessalonians 3:12
\p
\v 12 We command those fellow believers who are not working, and urge \add them\add* by the authority [MTY] of our Lord Jesus Christ, that they settle down and ◄support themselves by working/work to earn money to buy what they need►.
\s1 You others, do not stop doing what is right because you are discouraged.
\sr 2 Thessalonians 3:13
\p
\v 13 Fellow believers! Do not ever get tired of doing what is right!
\s1 Publicly identify any fellow believer who does not obey what we have written in this letter and do not associate with him.
\sr 2 Thessalonians 3:14-15
\p
\v 14 If any \add fellow believer refuses to work\add* and does not obey what I have written in this letter, ◄\add publicly\add* identify that person/tell the congregation what that person is doing►. Then do not associate with him, in order that he may become ashamed.
\v 15 Do not think of him as though he was \add your\add* enemy; instead, warn him as \add you would warn your other\add* fellow believers.
\s1 I pray that our Lord Jesus himself will give peace to you always and in every situation.
\sr 2 Thessalonians 3:16a
\p
\v 16  \add I pray that our\add* Lord \add Jesus\add* himself, who \add gives inner\add* peace \add to his people\add*, will give \add inner\add* peace to you always ◄and in every situation/whatever happens►.
\s1 In closing, I pray that our Lord Jesus will continue to bless you all. I, Paul, am greeting you and I am writing this myself in order that you may know that it is I who have sent this letter.
\sr 2 Thessalonians 3:16b-18
\p I \add pray that our\add* Lord \add Jesus will continue to\add* help you all.
\v 17 Now, having taken the pen from my scribe, I, Paul, am sending this greeting to you as I write this myself [SYN]. I do this in all my letters in order that you may know that it is truly I who have sent this letter. This is how I always end my letters.
\v 18 I pray that our Lord Jesus Christ will continue to act kindly to you all.
